PaymentRails_ExecuteActionNative
├── when the native key is not configured
│   └── it should revert with PaymentRails_TokenNotEnabled
├── when amount is zero
│   └── it should revert with PaymentRails_ZeroAmount
├── when amount is below minBalance
│   └── it should revert with PaymentRails_BelowMinimumBalance
├── when native balance is insufficient
│   └── it should revert with PaymentRails_InsufficientBalance
└── given a native route with sufficient balance
    ├── when the module succeeds
    │   ├── it should return true
    │   ├── it should push exactly amount of native to the module
    │   ├── it should leave the remaining native on paymentRails
    │   └── it should emit ActionExecuted with NATIVE_TOKEN as token
    ├── when the module reverts
    │   ├── it should return false
    │   ├── it should keep the native on paymentRails
    │   ├── it should emit NativeActionReverted with the revert data
    │   └── it should emit ActionFailed with "Module execution reverted"
    ├── when the module returns success false
    │   ├── it should revert with PaymentRails_NativeModuleReturnedFailure
    │   └── it should keep the native on paymentRails
    ├── when called by a non-owner
    │   └── it should succeed
    ├── given value arrived without calling receive
    │   └── it should route it
    ├── when amount equals the full balance
    │   └── it should drain paymentRails
    └── fuzz
        └── when amount is between minBalance and balance
            └── it should push exactly amount
